meta {
  name: 17. Cleanup - Delete Target DataStructure
  type: http
  seq: 28
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datastructures/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{pgTargetDataStructureId}}
}

tests {
  test("Target DataStructure deleted or already gone", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 204=deleted, 404=already gone
    expect(status === 204 || status === 404).to.be.true;
  });
}

docs {
  **PostGIS saga step 17** — Delete the target (geometry) DataStructure (cleanup).

  Deletes the target structure created in step 3. Must run after the DataSink (step 13) and dataset (step 15) are gone, since the POSTGIS DataSink referenced this structure's version. Deleting a released structure cascades its versions (no unrelease needed).

  **Expected Response:** 204 No Content. 404 if already deleted.

  **Post-condition:** Target DataStructure record removed from `portal_backend` DB.
}
